nolink "false"

\end_inset

 show the production term for O-atoms,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{R}_{O}=\left(\frac{C_{O}^{n+1}-C_{O}^{n}}{\Delta t}\right)W_{O}$
\end_inset

,
 at 
\begin_inset Formula $t=200\text{ }\mu$
\end_inset

s for 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

detonationEulerFoam
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 The OpenFOAM result of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{R}_{O}$
\end_inset

 using the seulex ODE solver is denoted as 
\begin_inset Formula $R_{of}$
\end_inset

 and the result using the ChemGen YASS ODE solver is denoted as 
\begin_inset Formula $R_{cg}$
\end_inset

 .
 These results demonstrate that an accurate CFD solution can be obtained using ChemGen in the 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

detonationEulerFoam
\end_layout

\end_inset

 solver.
 Furthermore,
 the YASS solver provided by ChemGen is found to be on average 8 times faster than the seulex solver.
\end_layout

